  "markdown": "# 3x4 Simultaneous ECG Report\n\n**Patient Details**\n- **Name**: John Sample\n- **ID**: 123123\n- **Gender**: Male\n- **Date of Birth**: 1/25/1950   (61 years)\n- **Height**: 6 ft 3 in\n- **Weight**: 223 lbs\n\n**Recording Details**\n- **Recorded**: 2/17/2011 2:21:27 PM\n- **Device**: CL   131568\n- **Location**: [blank]\n\n**Measurements**\n- **Heart Rate**: 80 bpm\n- **P Duration**: 102 ms\n- **PR Interval**: 186 ms\n- **QRS Duration**: 100 ms\n- **QT Interval**: 360 ms\n- **QTc Interval**: 416 ms\n- **P,QRS,T Axis**: 49°, 50°, 49°\n\n**Interpretation (Unconfirmed)**\n004 Normal sinus rhythm\n193 Anteroseptal infarction, probably old\n239 Ischemic ST-T changes in posterior leads\n\n**Comments:**\n\n<figure type=\"CHART\">Scale: 25.0 mm/s 10.0 mm/mV 5mm/sqr. Data must be reviewed by a qualified physician. Filters: 0.05 - 150 Hz<table><tr><th>Row</th><th>Leads</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>I, aVR, V1, V4</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>II, aVL, V2, V5</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>III, aVF, V3, V6</td></tr><tr><td>4 (rhythm strip)</td><td>II</td></tr></table>\n\n<description>A 12-lead electrocardiogram printed on a red grid background. It has three rows of four standard and augmented leads (I, aVR, V1, V4 in the top row; II, aVL, V2, V5 in the middle row; III, aVF, V3, V6 in the third row), with a full-width lead II rhythm strip at the bottom. Each row begins with a small rectangular calibration pulse at the left edge. Vertical red separators divide the leads into four columns. The traces show narrow, sharp QRS complexes with a regular repeating rhythm, each followed by a rounded T wave, with a flat baseline between beats. Amplitude varies by lead: lead aVL is nearly flat, while V1 and V2 show deeper negative deflections and aVR shows predominantly negative complexes.</description></figure>\n\nPage 1 of 9    Printed: Wednesday, March 02, 2011\n\nCopyright QRS Diagnostic\n\nML122 Rev.6/11\n\n<!-- doc_id=parse-01m7rsv97v8yxkvcv6zqf8negx -->",
